    "reading": {
        "body": "Uptime among tracked AI API providers is uneven: three report 100% healthy checks, while Lambda is lowest at 81.3% and OpenAI at 89.5%.\n\nThese figures come from automated checks against each provider's own reported status, not independent tests of live endpoints. That means they can lag or understate real user-facing disruptions, and short blips between checks may not appear. They are a directional reliability signal, not a service-level guarantee.\n\nMost providers cluster above 95% healthy, but the daily count of healthy providers falls to 10 on four days across the tracked window, indicating occasional multi-provider incidents. For AI workloads, API availability is a prerequisite for inference and model access, but this data says nothing about underlying compute capacity, power supply, or grid constraints.",
